      "content": "Thanks, that's a decent start. It's a bit on the shorter side though. The library ranking system is definitely going to favor much longer entries, so I'm worried this might get buried by other entries that provide more depth.\n\nCan you try to expand on this? I want a version that is significantly more exhaustive—go into the mathematical basis of the linear combination, explain the implications of the Copenhagen interpretation vs other interpretations, and maybe walk through the math of a simple two-state system. \n\nAgain, please don't just repeat what you already said or add fluff just to make it longer. I need actual substance, but it really needs to be a much more substantial read to hit a high score in our system.",
